  "summary": "Preinstall script exfiltrates host identifiers to interactsh OAST endpoint",
  "details": "The package's preinstall lifecycle script runs `whoami` and `hostname` locally, fetches the installer's public IP, and transmits all three as query parameters in a plaintext HTTP GET to a hardcoded `kwphewvexhjbtfduscqybx6q7c862eh0g.oast.fun` subdomain (interactsh out-of-band callback infrastructure). The behavior fires automatically on `npm install`. The README contradicts the observed code by stating the package makes no network requests. The collected fields (username, hostname, public IP) form a reconnaissance beacon consistent with dependency-confusion probing.",
